#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_perfect_number

#% text
# `is_perfect_number(k)` gives true when the integer k is a perfect number, the sum of its proper divisors: sigma_1(k) = 2 k.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is false for anything other than a positive integer.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_perfect_number(496)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
select(range(10000), is_perfect_number)
#% output
#= [6, 28, 496, 8128]

#% cell
is_perfect_number(2^(7 - 1)*(2^7 - 1))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_perfect_number(x)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `perfect_number`, `divisor_sigma`
